  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "2v1 back and forth – the shooter defends",
  "description": "Play across the rink: put two small goals facing each other at the long sides in one half. Split the players into two teams. Each team has a line behind its goal, and the game goes 2v1 back and forth across the rink.\n\nTwo blues attack against one red defender. When the attack ends – goal, save or puck out – the player who shot becomes the defender straight away. At the same time red starts the next attack: the red defender gets a pass from the team-mate behind the goal, and the two of them attack the other way against the shooter. The other blue attacker goes to their team's line. It keeps going without a break, with constant transitions and a high tempo.\n\nWith lots of players: set up the same game in the other half. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attackers: make yourselves available – wide and deep, not side by side."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Take on the defender so they have to choose, and pass once they have."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "After your shot: turn straight away – you are the defender now."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defender: close the shooting lane and force a pass."
    }
  ],
